  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Menton and Roquebrune-Cap-Martin, neighbours on the Italian border, form a compact area where you can stay in the centre or towards Garavan and reach the few beaches open to dogs on foot or by car. This page gathers useful pointers before booking; each hotel has its own listing, with its own rule.</p>

      <h2>The area's hotels on Coco Explore</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/fiche-hotel-mediterranee-menton">Best Western Hôtel Méditerranée</a>, Menton</li>
        <li><a href="/fiche-hebergement-hotel-menton-riviera-menton">Hôtel Menton Riviera</a>, Menton (French page)</li>
        <li><a href="/fiche-hebergement-hotel-royal-westminster-menton">Hôtel Royal Westminster</a>, Menton (French page)</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Beach rules are strict in Menton. The town's general beach regulations (2023 order, article 20) reserve two beaches for people accompanied by dogs, all year round: one east of the entrance to the Garavan marina, the other where the Careï stream meets the sea, facing the casino. They declare all other beaches prohibited to dogs, even on a leash, and swimming for dogs is also prohibited on the concession beaches. In its reminder of 29 April 2026, the town names three set-up beaches: Gorbio beach (boundary with Roquebrune-Cap-Martin), Casino beach and Hawaï beach (Garavan), marked out by sails and signs, and announces fines after a week of prevention. Its "Le bord de mer, les plages" page names only Hawaï and the Casino.</p>
      <p>In Roquebrune-Cap-Martin, the tourist office describes the Plage de la Piscine (promenade Robert Schuman, between the swimming pool and the town exit sign in the direction of Menton) as "specially for dogs", free and open all year in 2026. However, the municipal parks and gardens regulations do not admit pets in parks, lawns and play areas, even on a leash, except assistance dogs. The Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourism listing "Plages accessibles aux chiens" mentions, for Menton and Roquebrune, three beaches: a dog beach near the Italian border, the Casino beach and another just before the Bains du Cap.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the list of authorised beaches differs between the documents of the town, the tourist office and the Region; before laying down your towel, look at the signs and the sails marking out the zones.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Menton also has two fenced dog parks, avenue Blasco Ibanez and corniche Serres de la Madone (see <a href="/en/fiche-activite-parcs-canins-menton">Menton's dog parks</a>), and the <a href="/fiche-plage-casino-menton">Casino beach</a> (French page) has its own listing.</p>
